## Rules that apply everywhere

- **Never hardcode a color.** Every color/font is a Swift token in a `Theme/`
  directory — see `docs/ai/theming_rules.md`. `Scripts/check_hardcoded_colors.sh`
  blocks a commit that violates this.
- **Never hardcode a user-facing string.** Route through the owning module's
  `L10n.<key>` — see `docs/ai/ui_rules.md`.
- **A protocol is owned by its consumer, not its implementer** — see
  `docs/CODING_STANDARDS.md`'s protocol-boundary section (§8.2).
- **Use the Skills for routine work** — `/new-feature`, `/add-module`,
  `/add-permission`, etc. (`.claude/skills/`) — rather than hand-rolling folder
  structure or navigation wiring; they encode this project's locked-in decisions
  so you don't have to re-derive them.

